WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:10.093
[tense music playing]

2
00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:22.940
[John] I tried.

3
00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.108
I did. I put everything on the table.

4
00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:26.193
[person] No!

5
00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:28.570
[John] I tried my best.

6
00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:30.030
[person pants]

7
00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:31.990
[grunts]

8
00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:33.951
[John] But some people here
live by violence.

9
00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:38.288
- [person grunting]
- [John] And for them it seems…

10
00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.416
it's the only language they understand.

11
00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.796
[music fades]

12
00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.714
[theme song playing]

13
00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.816
[Tom] Sergey Ojeda?

14
00:01:48.692 --> 00:01:50.652
I'm telling you. I don't like it.
Bad idea.

15
00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:51.862
[John] You keep saying that.

16
00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.322
[Tom] Because I keep thinking it.

17
00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.700
Fucking Satan owes him money.

18
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.369
[John] Exactly.
He knows all the right people.

19
00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:01.288
[Tom] He'll want
his pound of flesh in return.

20
00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.834
Look. I say we take our chances.
put it in the system.

21
00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:09.295
You have the evidence.
more than just the video now.

22
00:02:09.378 --> 00:02:11.131
Sound the fucking alarms. man.

23
00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:13.842
Look. who's gonna come
running to the rescue? The cops?

24
00:02:14.468 --> 00:02:15.719
I mean… [chuckles]

25
00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.845
City Hall?

26
00:02:17.888 --> 00:02:22.643
You know? I mean. this Fire Sale goes way
above the head of some Sheriff's Deputy.

27
00:02:22.726 --> 00:02:25.729
[sighs] If we make
the wrong decision. Tom.

28
00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:27.648
Danny's dead.

29
00:02:30.651 --> 00:02:31.860
[groans]

30
00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:38.617
Vega's got me in a corner.

31
00:02:41.203 --> 00:02:43.747
We're out of time. I need Sergey on this.

32
00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:45.582
Make the call.

33
00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:48.919
Set it up. I'm gonna go see Danny.
Make sure he's okay.

34
00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:53.549
All right. start your engines.

35
00:02:57.177 --> 00:03:01.014
Remember. that's Sheriff's territory.
They'll be listening.

36
00:03:01.098 --> 00:03:03.350
- Yeah. Eyes and ears.
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

37
00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:06.478
See ya.

38
00:03:07.938 --> 00:03:08.939
[Tom coughs]

39
00:03:14.403 --> 00:03:16.780
- [person] Vera Novak?
- So what if I am?

40
00:03:17.531 --> 00:03:19.449
- Got something for you.
- Yeah?

41
00:03:21.577 --> 00:03:22.911
Eyes and ears.

42
00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:26.456
[phone ringing]

43
00:03:29.877 --> 00:03:32.004
- Vega.
- [John] I wanna see him.

44
00:03:32.087 --> 00:03:33.797
[Vega] And I wanna see Ji. Tomorrow.

45
00:03:33.881 --> 00:03:35.841
[John] All right. before I do anything.
I wanna see him.

46
00:03:35.924 --> 00:03:37.301
I wanna make sure he's okay.

47
00:03:37.384 --> 00:03:39.511
Yeah. you have my word on that. but okay.

48
00:03:39.595 --> 00:03:41.638
- Come on down.
- I'm on my way.

49
00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:46.018
[line beeping]

50
00:03:57.362 --> 00:03:58.572
[Vega] Rabineau!

51
00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:13.504
[deputy] Door!

52
00:04:38.195 --> 00:04:39.446
[John] Hey.

53
00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.114
- Hey.
- [John] How you doin'?

54
00:04:41.198 --> 00:04:42.199
I'm all right.

55
00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:43.408
[John] Yeah?

56
00:04:43.492 --> 00:04:45.994
Yeah. I didn't sleep much.
but I'll be fine.

57
00:04:46.078 --> 00:04:47.496
It's good to see you.

58
00:04:47.579 --> 00:04:50.082
[Danny] Thanks for coming. man.
Sorry you had to come out this way.

59
00:04:50.165 --> 00:04:52.042
I must be one of
your worst clients ever. huh?

60
00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.545
No. Danny. you're not. Not at all.

61
00:04:54.628 --> 00:04:57.714
[Danny] Yeah. but I don't pay you.
I pick fights. I don't listen.

62
00:04:57.798 --> 00:04:59.258
You make me count my suits.

63
00:04:59.341 --> 00:05:02.010
Well. you should have been
keeping track from the start.

64
00:05:02.094 --> 00:05:03.220
That's true.

65
00:05:03.929 --> 00:05:05.013
So. uh…

66
00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.268
We have a problem.

67
00:05:10.102 --> 00:05:12.896
What do you…
What do you mean? Is… Is Ji okay?

68
00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:14.690
Yeah. he's all right. For now.

69
00:05:14.773 --> 00:05:17.609
But all this. you being in jail.
being arrested.

70
00:05:17.693 --> 00:05:18.902
It's a pretense.

71
00:05:18.986 --> 00:05:20.779
This is all about Ji and Vega.

72
00:05:21.446 --> 00:05:22.739
He knows about Ji?

73
00:05:24.741 --> 00:05:26.660
[stammers] Okay. then.
What is he doing. the cop?

74
00:05:26.743 --> 00:05:27.744
What does he want?

75
00:05:27.828 --> 00:05:29.621
Danny. listen to me.
You're gonna have to trust me. okay?

76
00:05:29.705 --> 00:05:31.415
What the fuck does he want. Sugar?

77
00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:34.543
He wants to trade.

78
00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.461
[Danny] What?

79
00:05:36.545 --> 00:05:39.548
- [deputy] Moon. Wrap it up.
- Hold on. I just got here.

80
00:05:39.631 --> 00:05:41.842
- You're not gonna do it. though. right?
- Danny. listen to me.

81
00:05:41.925 --> 00:05:42.926
[Danny] No. please. I--

82
00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.387
- [deputy] Time to go.
- Yo. just-- I'm serious. you can't do it.

83
00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.056
Danny. listen. no matter what happens.
no matter what it looks like…

84
00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.309
Do not trade… [grunts]
Whoa! I just fucking--

85
00:05:50.392 --> 00:05:52.394
- Hey! Hey!
- [Danny] No. do not do it!

86
00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:54.229
Sugar. do not do it!

87
00:05:54.313 --> 00:05:56.732
- All right. all right! All right!
- [deputy muttering]

88
00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:58.358
[Danny] Don't!

89
00:05:58.442 --> 00:06:00.319
[screams. grunts]

90
00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:03.864
[phone ringing]

91
00:06:05.449 --> 00:06:07.159
[John] Hey. Stanley. what's up?

92
00:06:07.242 --> 00:06:10.954
[Stanley] Uh. I am so sorry
to bother you. I…

93
00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:13.332
- [John] You okay?
- Um…

94
00:06:13.415 --> 00:06:17.294
I didn't know who… who to call. so I just…

95
00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:18.712
[John] All right. Where are you?

96
00:06:21.006 --> 00:06:22.716
Just a silly bird.

97
00:06:22.799 --> 00:06:24.301
No. you loved him.

98
00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:27.346
My daughters are grown. gone away.

99
00:06:27.429 --> 00:06:31.183
My wife left me
for a humanities professor.

100
00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:32.351
Humanities.

101
00:06:33.185 --> 00:06:34.561
Whatever that is.

102
00:06:38.941 --> 00:06:41.568
Do you notice… notice the spines?

103
00:06:45.364 --> 00:06:49.451
Yeah. 'cause that's how they protect
themselves from the herbivores.

104
00:06:54.915 --> 00:06:57.292
There's a Picasso quote about youth…

105
00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:02.005
Uh. some… I'm trying to remember it.

106
00:07:04.091 --> 00:07:07.135
[sighs] You know. my mind. uh…

107
00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:10.138
You wanna sit down?

108
00:07:10.222 --> 00:07:11.849
That would be good. [sighs]

109
00:07:11.932 --> 00:07:13.058
Come on.

110
00:07:14.268 --> 00:07:15.727
Oh. man.

111
00:07:15.811 --> 00:07:16.937
[sighs]

112
00:07:22.568 --> 00:07:25.320
Stanley. I'm not a tax attorney.

113
00:07:26.113 --> 00:07:28.115
- What?
- I don't live in Covina.

114
00:07:29.283 --> 00:07:30.701
Okay. where do you live?

115
00:07:31.285 --> 00:07:34.746
I wanna… I wanna talk to you. Stanley.
I wanna talk to you about Senator Pavich.

116
00:07:37.958 --> 00:07:38.959
- Pavich?
- Yeah.

117
00:07:39.042 --> 00:07:40.586
he hired you to work
on something with him.

118
00:07:40.669 --> 00:07:43.130
It's a project of some kind.

119
00:07:44.965 --> 00:07:46.800
[sniffs. clears throat]
Sorry to disappoint you.

120
00:07:46.884 --> 00:07:49.219
whoever you are.
but. uh. I'm not gonna tell you.

121
00:07:49.303 --> 00:07:51.013
Yes. you are. Stanley.

122
00:07:51.096 --> 00:07:52.973
Stanley. Stanley. wait. listen to me.

123
00:07:55.058 --> 00:07:56.059
Please.

124
00:07:58.103 --> 00:08:03.442
So. talking about TV shows.
caring about plants.

125
00:08:05.068 --> 00:08:08.906
pretending like you give a shit about
my parrot. Monty. that-that was all a lie?

126
00:08:08.989 --> 00:08:09.990
No.

127
00:08:10.991 --> 00:08:14.036
It wasn't a lie.
I enjoyed being your friend. I still do.

128
00:08:14.536 --> 00:08:16.455
I like you so much. Stanley.
I just need your help.

129
00:08:16.538 --> 00:08:17.539
[sighs]

130
00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:19.791
All right. the four circles.

131
00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:21.418
What are they?

132
00:08:22.085 --> 00:08:24.296
They keep turning up.
I don't know what they mean.

133
00:08:27.216 --> 00:08:31.637
I think Pavich. with the help of
a man named Henry Thorpe…

134
00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:36.058
I think he betrayed
a lot of people that I love.

135
00:08:39.144 --> 00:08:42.688
He forced them into hiding. and I…
I don't know why.

136
00:08:42.773 --> 00:08:44.650
I don't know why.
I don't know what happened.

137
00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:49.321
but I think it's gotta do with
these four circles. and I need your help.

138
00:08:50.614 --> 00:08:51.782
[sighs]

139
00:08:55.327 --> 00:08:56.995
Please. The four circles.

140
00:09:02.668 --> 00:09:03.669
[sighs]

141
00:09:04.169 --> 00:09:05.379
They're not circles.

142
00:09:05.462 --> 00:09:10.008
[stammers]
The circles are tropospheric nodes.

143
00:09:10.092 --> 00:09:11.677
Tropospheric nodes?

144
00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.762
[tense music playing]

145
00:09:17.391 --> 00:09:20.143
- To be used as what? A weapon?
- No.

146
00:09:20.227 --> 00:09:21.812
Not at all. No. it's to help the climate.

147
00:09:21.895 --> 00:09:23.438
[thunderclap]

148
00:09:23.522 --> 00:09:25.816
- To help the climate in what way?
- Whatever way we want.

149
00:09:25.899 --> 00:09:27.234
[beeping]

150
00:09:27.317 --> 00:09:30.112
Dispel greenhouse gases.

151
00:09:30.195 --> 00:09:32.990
raise O2. lower CO2.

152
00:09:33.907 --> 00:09:35.659
optimize crop yields.

153
00:09:36.285 --> 00:09:39.705
suppress wildfires. prevent flash floods.
and on and on.

154
00:09:41.415 --> 00:09:43.959
John. this can change the world.

155
00:09:44.668 --> 00:09:45.878
Literally.

156
00:09:45.961 --> 00:09:47.171
You invented this?

157
00:09:47.254 --> 00:09:49.715
Oh. my good God. no.
I'm just one of the engineers.

158
00:09:51.383 --> 00:09:54.803
[stammers]
I helped to scale it up. put it together.

159
00:09:54.887 --> 00:09:56.555
I've theorized about…

160
00:09:56.638 --> 00:10:01.935
But this technology is beyond
another level. It's not a weapon.

161
00:10:02.019 --> 00:10:03.270
No. I-I would never…

162
00:10:03.353 --> 00:10:04.688
Yeah. but it scares you.

163
00:10:06.148 --> 00:10:10.068
It does. I've seen it on your face.
Even now. you're… you're conflicted. Why?

164
00:10:10.736 --> 00:10:12.696
Yeah. well. we have to do something.

165
00:10:14.072 --> 00:10:18.911
[stammering] The planet's dying!
The world's on fire because of us.

166
00:10:19.578 --> 00:10:20.746
That's what scares me.

167
00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:25.918
But yes. a power like this? Playing God?

168
00:10:26.001 --> 00:10:28.879
You'd be a fool not to be scared. so--

169
00:10:28.962 --> 00:10:31.131
[phone buzzing]

170
00:10:32.549 --> 00:10:34.801
- [John] I have to take this--
- I'm-I'm gonna be leaving now.

171
00:10:34.885 --> 00:10:35.886
[stammers] Stanley…

172
00:10:38.472 --> 00:10:39.598
- Hey.
- [Tom] All set.

173
00:10:39.681 --> 00:10:42.559
- You're on with Sergey. Be careful.
- All right. good.

174
00:10:42.643 --> 00:10:44.102
[line ringing]

175
00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.774
- [Val] What's up?
- How's Ji?

176
00:10:48.857 --> 00:10:52.110
You know. bitching and moaning
like he's the one in jail.

177
00:10:52.194 --> 00:10:54.154
Well. he's detoxing. you know?

178
00:10:54.238 --> 00:10:55.697
Mood swings are normal.

179
00:10:55.781 --> 00:10:57.324
Yep. I know all about it.

180
00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.410
It's important you're there. Val.

181
00:11:00.494 --> 00:11:02.704
All right. I need you
to keep an eye on him.

182
00:11:02.788 --> 00:11:05.207
- All right. Boss.
- All right. I gotta go.

183
00:11:05.707 --> 00:11:07.084
I'll call you later. okay?

184
00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.936
- Mr. Sugar. What a pleasure.
- [John] Diego.

185
00:11:26.019 --> 00:11:29.022
I was in my office doing God knows what

186
00:11:29.106 --> 00:11:31.817
when Papa comes in to tell me
that you reached out to him.

187
00:11:32.359 --> 00:11:34.236
[chuckles] His face.

188
00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.488
He was so happy.

189
00:11:37.281 --> 00:11:38.282
May I?

190
00:11:42.119 --> 00:11:44.329
You know I don't carry a weapon. Diego.

191
00:11:44.413 --> 00:11:45.414
I know.

192
00:11:46.373 --> 00:11:47.708
I'm sorry.

193
00:11:48.375 --> 00:11:49.710
It's for precautions.

194
00:11:59.761 --> 00:12:01.471
[John] Sergey Ojeda.

195
00:12:01.555 --> 00:12:04.183
Head of a cartel called Los Universales.

196
00:12:04.808 --> 00:12:07.895
which. loosely translated.
means "we're everywhere."

197
00:12:09.229 --> 00:12:11.481
I did a job for him once. years ago.

198
00:12:12.232 --> 00:12:14.067
Of course. he would say
I did half a job for him.

199
00:12:14.151 --> 00:12:16.987
and he is not a man you do half a job for.

200
00:12:21.074 --> 00:12:22.409
You look good.

201
00:12:23.535 --> 00:12:25.621
- Thanks.
- Sit.

202
00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:35.714
How do I look?

203
00:12:39.051 --> 00:12:40.385
- Old.
- [scoffs]

204
00:12:40.469 --> 00:12:41.887
[speaks Spanish]

205
00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:45.182
[scoffs] Look. I'm trying
to be nice to you. Hmm?

206
00:12:45.974 --> 00:12:47.100
You came to me.

207
00:12:47.684 --> 00:12:49.520
Don't you want me to be nice to you?

208
00:12:49.603 --> 00:12:52.648
I suppose. but it's inessential.

209
00:12:52.731 --> 00:12:54.525
You have things you want done.

210
00:12:55.817 --> 00:12:58.111
and sometimes
it's in my ability to do them.

211
00:12:58.195 --> 00:13:00.113
You know.
our relationship is transactional.

212
00:13:00.614 --> 00:13:04.076
Seems to me that. in the past.
that's when trouble came.

213
00:13:04.743 --> 00:13:06.119
You know. when we forgot that.

214
00:13:07.829 --> 00:13:09.373
You're honest with me.

215
00:13:10.165 --> 00:13:13.544
I didn't always agree with you.
but. uh. you are.

216
00:13:16.839 --> 00:13:19.091
It is a rare quality.

217
00:13:25.639 --> 00:13:28.433
Do you know this. uh. uh. Bad Bunny?

218
00:13:29.852 --> 00:13:30.978
I've heard of him.

219
00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:34.940
I'm meeting my granddaughter in Miami.
uh. to see him.

220
00:13:35.023 --> 00:13:36.024
Nice.

221
00:13:36.567 --> 00:13:39.403
She's sweet. but. uh…
not looking forward to it.

222
00:13:42.489 --> 00:13:44.408
So. uh. a policeman?

223
00:13:44.491 --> 00:13:45.868
Uh. what is his. uh--

224
00:13:45.951 --> 00:13:47.744
Ray Vega. He works for you.

225
00:13:48.245 --> 00:13:50.581
He's an enforcer
for your Fire Sale business.

226
00:13:52.165 --> 00:13:54.585
So many businesses.
uh. in over 50 countries--

227
00:13:54.668 --> 00:13:58.046
Yeah. identity theft. housing fraud.
and building kickbacks.

228
00:13:59.715 --> 00:14:01.884
Hundreds of millions in federal contracts.

229
00:14:02.426 --> 00:14:04.511
all on the backs of
the homeless and the addicted.

230
00:14:04.595 --> 00:14:07.347
I mean. it's a nasty business. Sergey.
even by your standards.

231
00:14:07.431 --> 00:14:08.432
[speaks Spanish]

232
00:14:08.515 --> 00:14:11.059
[scoffs] John.
the whole world is a nasty business.

233
00:14:11.143 --> 00:14:13.103
Let's not have that argument again.

234
00:14:13.187 --> 00:14:14.188
Please?

235
00:14:15.147 --> 00:14:16.565
[clears throat]

236
00:14:19.359 --> 00:14:22.821
So. what do you want me to do
with this policeman?

237
00:14:22.905 --> 00:14:24.740
- Uh. I kill him?
- No. no. no.

238
00:14:24.823 --> 00:14:27.993
- He's got a client of mine in jail.
- Ah.

239
00:14:28.076 --> 00:14:31.705
And he's been trying to squeeze me.
so. you know. just get him to back off.

240
00:14:32.247 --> 00:14:33.540
Let my client out.

241
00:14:36.543 --> 00:14:37.669
That's all?

242
00:14:38.754 --> 00:14:39.796
That's it.

243
00:14:40.631 --> 00:14:41.673
And me?

244
00:14:42.841 --> 00:14:44.134
What do I get?

245
00:14:52.351 --> 00:14:53.852
I'll finish the job.

246
00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:01.235
Adiós.

247
00:15:01.318 --> 00:15:02.569
[speaks Spanish]

248
00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:04.988
[tense music playing]

249
00:15:10.786 --> 00:15:15.290
[John] And just like that.
I'm back in business with Sergey Ojeda.

250
00:15:20.295 --> 00:15:21.505
[line ringing]

251
00:15:25.259 --> 00:15:27.427
Looks like someone went crying to Dad.

252
00:15:27.511 --> 00:15:29.221
We do what we gotta do. Ray.

253
00:15:29.763 --> 00:15:30.764
Release him.

254
00:15:30.848 --> 00:15:32.933
[laughs] Release him?

255
00:15:33.016 --> 00:15:35.686
You're watching too many movies. Sugar.
Nobody talks like that.

256
00:15:35.769 --> 00:15:38.856
It's over. Ray. Sergey can have you
in a barrel at the bottom of the ocean

257
00:15:38.939 --> 00:15:40.315
without blinking an eye.

258
00:15:41.149 --> 00:15:44.236
All right. Now. it's gonna take you
a minute to. uh. cover your tracks.

259
00:15:44.319 --> 00:15:46.947
So. dummy your paperwork.
do what you gotta do.

260
00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:49.283
But I want Danny out.
and I want him out tonight.

261
00:15:50.033 --> 00:15:51.034
It's over.

262
00:15:52.119 --> 00:15:53.453
[line beeping]

263
00:16:12.347 --> 00:16:13.557
[phone ringing]

264
00:16:18.729 --> 00:16:19.938
Yep.

265
00:16:20.022 --> 00:16:22.858
[Charlotte] You know.
I realized I don't have your number.

266
00:16:22.941 --> 00:16:26.069
- Not many do.
- I see. Dinner?

267
00:16:26.153 --> 00:16:30.073
[John] Uh. it's not even 5:00.
The restaurant ain't open yet.

268
00:16:30.157 --> 00:16:33.911
Ah. okay. So. room service?

269
00:16:33.994 --> 00:16:34.995
Yours or mine?

270
00:16:35.495 --> 00:16:37.497
[piano music playing]

271
00:17:01.188 --> 00:17:03.190
[water whooshing]

272
00:17:13.742 --> 00:17:18.539
[Charlotte] "We wind along the Pacific
Coast Highway turning west once more.

273
00:17:19.373 --> 00:17:22.416
The ocean now forever
in your view as you move

274
00:17:22.501 --> 00:17:27.673
along the breezy byways
toward historic San Simeon."

275
00:17:27.756 --> 00:17:29.508
"Breezy byways…"

276
00:17:29.591 --> 00:17:31.552
Hmm. Sounds lovely.

277
00:17:34.763 --> 00:17:36.515
[piano music continues]

278
00:17:42.145 --> 00:17:43.397
Cactus.

279
00:17:44.356 --> 00:17:47.609
Yeah. uh… A friend of mine gave it to me.

280
00:17:47.693 --> 00:17:49.444
- It's sweet.
- Mmm.

281
00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:54.074
My room doesn't have a record player.

282
00:17:54.157 --> 00:17:56.034
Why did you get a record player?

283
00:17:56.118 --> 00:17:57.369
I don't know.

284
00:17:57.452 --> 00:17:59.288
Do you own any records?

285
00:17:59.371 --> 00:18:00.831
I do not.

286
00:18:00.914 --> 00:18:02.833
And yet you get the record player?

287
00:18:02.916 --> 00:18:04.293
Doesn't seem fair.

288
00:18:06.795 --> 00:18:08.255
Where are you from?

289
00:18:08.338 --> 00:18:11.008
Ooh. Questions. Here we go.

290
00:18:11.925 --> 00:18:14.720
Merion. Pennsylvania.
Just outside Philadelphia.

291
00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:17.681
Brothers? Sisters?

292
00:18:17.764 --> 00:18:19.474
No brothers. no sisters. no kids.

293
00:18:20.058 --> 00:18:21.059
Just me.

294
00:18:21.143 --> 00:18:22.477
Parents?

295
00:18:22.561 --> 00:18:23.562
We don't talk.

296
00:18:24.438 --> 00:18:25.439
How come?

297
00:18:26.148 --> 00:18:27.691
A million reasons. [sighs]

298
00:18:28.901 --> 00:18:30.694
They don't like what I do.

299
00:18:30.777 --> 00:18:33.697
They don't like
passionate humanitarianism?

300
00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:35.282
[chuckles] Can you believe it?

301
00:18:35.991 --> 00:18:37.117
They're conservative.

302
00:18:37.201 --> 00:18:38.202
Ah.

303
00:18:38.785 --> 00:18:44.499
They want me to live
in some world of years gone by…

304
00:18:44.583 --> 00:18:46.960
[inhales deeply] When everything was…

305
00:18:47.044 --> 00:18:48.337
I don't know what.

306
00:18:49.046 --> 00:18:50.380
Uncomplicated?

307
00:18:51.632 --> 00:18:55.177
But I can't do that. and I won't do that.
so we don't talk.

308
00:18:57.095 --> 00:18:58.388
I'm sorry.

309
00:18:59.848 --> 00:19:01.433
I shouldn't be telling you this.
[chuckles]

310
00:19:01.517 --> 00:19:03.810
No. wh-why shouldn't you
be telling me this?

311
00:19:03.894 --> 00:19:06.480
[chuckles] 'Cause you're a stranger.

312
00:19:06.563 --> 00:19:08.190
I only just got your phone number.

313
00:19:08.273 --> 00:19:09.733
[chuckles]

314
00:19:09.816 --> 00:19:12.486
- And my favorite ice cream is mint chip.
- Noted.

315
00:19:13.946 --> 00:19:15.656
Your turn. Where are you from?

316
00:19:18.367 --> 00:19:21.620
- Can we skip that one?
- What? That's like the easiest one.

317
00:19:21.703 --> 00:19:24.498
No. pistachio being my favorite
ice cream is much easier.

318
00:19:24.581 --> 00:19:25.874
[inhales sharply] Family?

319
00:19:26.458 --> 00:19:28.043
Uh. sister.

320
00:19:29.086 --> 00:19:30.087
Djen.

321
00:19:30.587 --> 00:19:31.713
What's she like?

322
00:19:32.256 --> 00:19:33.507
She's. uh…

323
00:19:35.092 --> 00:19:36.260
She's not…

324
00:19:39.513 --> 00:19:42.099
She was… She was smart.

325
00:19:43.517 --> 00:19:44.768
Beyond anything.

326
00:19:44.852 --> 00:19:45.853
She was…

327
00:19:45.936 --> 00:19:48.981
Loved puzzles. you know. solving problems.

328
00:19:50.482 --> 00:19:51.817
and she was opinionated.

329
00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:56.196
[inhales deeply] I mean. she had
her opinions. and she wouldn't rest…

330
00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:59.157
[gulps] …until you saw things her way.

331
00:20:00.075 --> 00:20:03.412
Which you might have
because she was so convincing.

332
00:20:04.746 --> 00:20:05.747
Yeah.

333
00:20:06.456 --> 00:20:07.708
She was kind.

334
00:20:09.042 --> 00:20:11.962
Loving. You know.
she could be so loving. but tough too.

335
00:20:13.422 --> 00:20:14.923
I think the first memory I have…

336
00:20:15.966 --> 00:20:19.344
The first kind of feeling
I can recall is just

337
00:20:20.554 --> 00:20:22.431
you know. not wanting to let her down.

338
00:20:23.557 --> 00:20:24.850
She was…

339
00:20:26.018 --> 00:20:27.519
She was something.

340
00:20:29.855 --> 00:20:32.274
What… What happened to her?

341
00:20:34.318 --> 00:20:35.569
I don't know.

342
00:20:36.778 --> 00:20:38.197
She just… She died.

343
00:20:42.701 --> 00:20:43.827
I'm sorry.

344
00:20:44.494 --> 00:20:45.787
That's terrible.

345
00:20:46.538 --> 00:20:48.624
Yeah. It is.

346
00:20:49.458 --> 00:20:53.086
[inhales deeply] Yeah.

347
00:21:01.762 --> 00:21:03.180
You wanna get an ice cream with me?

348
00:21:07.809 --> 00:21:09.478
- Hell yeah.
- Yeah?

349
00:21:09.561 --> 00:21:10.562
- Yeah.
- All right.

350
00:21:10.646 --> 00:21:12.064
Let's do that.

351
00:21:12.147 --> 00:21:14.233
["I Like the Way You Love Me" playing]

352
00:21:31.041 --> 00:21:32.292
[music ends]

353
00:21:35.462 --> 00:21:37.464
[phone buzzing]

354
00:21:51.436 --> 00:21:53.397
- Tom?
- [Tom] Sergey's dead.

355
00:21:54.022 --> 00:21:56.024
[tense music playing]

356
00:21:57.776 --> 00:22:00.279
- Can you meet?
- Yep. I'm in the lobby.

357
00:22:00.362 --> 00:22:02.614
- [line beeping]
- [sighs]

358
00:22:04.741 --> 00:22:06.076
[grunts]

359
00:22:06.159 --> 00:22:11.498
So. yeah. a plane went down
near Lake Charles en route to Miami.

360
00:22:12.165 --> 00:22:16.086
Some fog in the area. some lightning.
but too soon to know anything yet.

361
00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:18.297
They know no survivors. right?
You said no survivors?

362
00:22:18.380 --> 00:22:19.464
That they do know.

363
00:22:20.841 --> 00:22:22.342
He's dead. the crew.

364
00:22:25.596 --> 00:22:28.599
What about Diego? The son?

365
00:22:28.682 --> 00:22:31.310
- He always travels with him.
- Uh. let's see.

366
00:22:32.686 --> 00:22:33.896
I bet he wasn't on the plane.

367
00:22:33.979 --> 00:22:36.273
I got three killed. was told two crew.

368
00:22:36.356 --> 00:22:37.900
- So. yeah. you win that bet.
- [sighs]

369
00:22:40.319 --> 00:22:41.486
- [coughs]
- [chuckles]

370
00:22:42.779 --> 00:22:44.573
Fire Sale's Diego.

371
00:22:46.325 --> 00:22:48.952
It's not Sergey. it was never Sergey.
Why didn't I know that?

372
00:22:49.036 --> 00:22:50.329
I should have known that.

373
00:22:50.412 --> 00:22:51.788
Okay. so you're good. not perfect.

374
00:22:51.872 --> 00:22:54.750
Yeah. I know. I know.
But Danny's not gettin' out now. Tom.

375
00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:58.712
You understand that?
I gotta meet Vega with an answer before…

376
00:22:58.795 --> 00:22:59.880
In eight hours.

377
00:22:59.963 --> 00:23:00.964
So. yeah.

378
00:23:03.675 --> 00:23:04.676
[sighs]

379
00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:06.929
[Tom] Talk to me. brother. What can I do?

380
00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:12.559
I don't know.

381
00:23:17.231 --> 00:23:18.649
[breathing heavily]

382
00:23:20.609 --> 00:23:21.985
Sergey was never a sure thing.

383
00:23:22.069 --> 00:23:25.864
[mutters] Um. I mean. we-we knew that.

384
00:23:26.782 --> 00:23:29.243
So. I guess now we… we go to plan B.

385
00:23:29.326 --> 00:23:30.327
[gunshot]

386
00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:31.411
[Tom] Okay. good.

387
00:23:31.495 --> 00:23:32.621
[tense music playing]

388
00:23:42.005 --> 00:23:43.423
Hey. it's gonna work out.

389
00:23:43.924 --> 00:23:46.176
It was always gonna go this way. right?

390
00:23:48.095 --> 00:23:50.681
[breathes deeply] Yeah. I know. I know.

391
00:23:50.764 --> 00:23:52.474
[breathes shakily]

392
00:24:00.148 --> 00:24:01.733
[Ji] I was the fighter first. you know?

393
00:24:02.317 --> 00:24:03.735
Way before Danny.

394
00:24:05.070 --> 00:24:06.780
Youth Sectionals.

395
00:24:06.864 --> 00:24:08.282
Youth Regionals.

396
00:24:08.365 --> 00:24:12.828
[inhales deeply] This dude once said
I could be the next Myung-Woo Yuh.

397
00:24:12.911 --> 00:24:15.706
[chuckles] Maybe the next Pacquiao.

398
00:24:16.456 --> 00:24:19.126
- The hype was real. you know?
- You keep fucking shooting me.

399
00:24:19.209 --> 00:24:20.252
Oh. sorry.

400
00:24:23.714 --> 00:24:26.049
But I fucked it up. [sighs]

401
00:24:26.133 --> 00:24:30.596
Broke my hand. and so. you know.
"Here's some meds for that."

402
00:24:30.679 --> 00:24:32.806
Then I had this other shit going on.

403
00:24:32.890 --> 00:24:37.811
like. Ma getting cancer
and Dad being a whatever.

404
00:24:37.895 --> 00:24:42.024
Then I broke my hand again and.
"Here's some more shit for that."

405
00:24:42.107 --> 00:24:43.567
and so on and so on.

406
00:24:43.650 --> 00:24:46.320
- You guys been doing this all night?
- Don't look at me.

407
00:24:46.945 --> 00:24:48.739
Insomnia. bro. I can't sleep.

408
00:24:50.449 --> 00:24:52.701
[sighs] I still had Danny.

409
00:24:53.285 --> 00:24:56.580
Being with him and seeing his life go.

410
00:24:57.998 --> 00:25:00.083
It's the only good thing I have left.

411
00:25:01.335 --> 00:25:04.046
- About to fuck that up too.
- No. you're not. You'll be fine.

412
00:25:04.129 --> 00:25:05.506
Everything I touch turns to shit.

413
00:25:05.589 --> 00:25:07.674
Fuckin' A. man. You sound like my sister.

414
00:25:07.758 --> 00:25:08.759
Sister?

415
00:25:08.842 --> 00:25:10.511
All your excuses set up in a row.

416
00:25:11.136 --> 00:25:12.554
My mom. my hand. my pills.

417
00:25:13.931 --> 00:25:17.267
Like you're the only person in history of
the fuckin' world that goes through shit.

418
00:25:17.351 --> 00:25:20.395
So everyone needs to feel fuckin'
bad for you and pick up your mess.

419
00:25:21.396 --> 00:25:23.065
- Fuckin' baby.
- Whoa.

420
00:25:23.148 --> 00:25:25.901
Do you know what Sugar's
getting ready to do for you right now?

421
00:25:27.069 --> 00:25:28.946
What he's willing to sacrifice for you?

422
00:25:29.530 --> 00:25:30.531
Why?

423
00:25:32.115 --> 00:25:33.909
Because you're such a great person?

424
00:25:37.037 --> 00:25:39.289
'Cause he's willing to do
something for someone else.

425
00:25:41.083 --> 00:25:42.376
You should really try it sometime.

426
00:25:43.293 --> 00:25:45.170
You're a fuckin' bitch. man.

427
00:25:45.254 --> 00:25:47.965
[inhales] Well. you're a fuckin' loser.

428
00:25:48.549 --> 00:25:50.217
Rather be a loser than a fuckin' bitch.

429
00:25:50.300 --> 00:25:52.302
Spoken like a fuckin' loser.

430
00:25:52.386 --> 00:25:54.388
[gunshots on TV]

431
00:25:55.305 --> 00:25:56.306
Dude.

432
00:25:58.517 --> 00:26:00.185
Dude. You gotta cover me.

433
00:26:44.605 --> 00:26:46.023
[John sighs]

434
00:26:48.400 --> 00:26:50.611
[sighs. mutters]

435
00:26:50.694 --> 00:26:51.904
No brother?

436
00:26:52.696 --> 00:26:54.072
We're not doing that.

437
00:26:54.156 --> 00:26:55.449
No? What are we doing?

438
00:27:12.883 --> 00:27:14.051
Panamanian passports. huh?

439
00:27:14.134 --> 00:27:16.094
[John] Yeah. there's one for you.
one for your daughter.

440
00:27:16.178 --> 00:27:18.764
There's also one for your ex-wife
in case you want her to join you.

441
00:27:20.098 --> 00:27:21.600
[chuckles]

442
00:27:25.938 --> 00:27:28.482
That's the deed to a villa
in Playa Coronado.

443
00:27:28.565 --> 00:27:30.609
It used to belong to a friend of mine.
He no longer needs it.

444
00:27:30.692 --> 00:27:32.611
Now. it's beautiful. It's on the beach.

445
00:27:32.694 --> 00:27:34.112
Golf course down the road.

446
00:27:36.114 --> 00:27:38.283
- That's a bank account.
- "Banco Banistmo."

447
00:27:38.825 --> 00:27:40.244
[John] Yeah. 'cause money's important.

448
00:27:44.039 --> 00:27:45.666
[chuckles]

449
00:27:45.749 --> 00:27:46.917
It's a real offer.

450
00:27:48.460 --> 00:27:49.586
It's a bribe.

451
00:27:50.879 --> 00:27:52.130
That's not the way I mean it.

452
00:27:53.131 --> 00:27:54.132
Everyone's good.

453
00:27:55.592 --> 00:27:58.220
You know.
that's what I was taught. [sighs]

454
00:27:58.303 --> 00:28:00.180
At the beginning. everyone's pure.

455
00:28:02.015 --> 00:28:04.518
And then life happens to us.
and we go out into the world

456
00:28:04.601 --> 00:28:07.604
and maybe we make choices
that lead us from our true selves.

457
00:28:08.981 --> 00:28:13.151
And if we don't… [sighs]
…turn back from those choices in time.

458
00:28:13.235 --> 00:28:15.654
if we don't turn it around.

459
00:28:17.281 --> 00:28:20.200
you know. we're… we're changed forever.

460
00:28:28.542 --> 00:28:30.460
This is a chance to turn it around. Ray.

461
00:28:40.387 --> 00:28:41.972
You know. it's true what you're saying.

462
00:28:44.224 --> 00:28:46.018
A lot of it. It's true.

463
00:28:50.355 --> 00:28:51.356
Yeah.

464
00:28:53.567 --> 00:28:57.988
I remember the look on my pop's face
the day that I graduated from the academy.

465
00:28:58.071 --> 00:29:01.325
Man. he'd been waiting so long
just to be proud of me.

466
00:29:06.872 --> 00:29:08.498
But that one moment. you know. It's…

467
00:29:09.666 --> 00:29:11.001
You were on the right side of things.

468
00:29:14.630 --> 00:29:15.964
You could be again.

469
00:29:17.591 --> 00:29:19.218
You had potential. You still do.

470
00:29:27.267 --> 00:29:28.936
[chuckles]

471
00:29:29.019 --> 00:29:30.687
Take it. Take it and walk.

472
00:29:33.315 --> 00:29:34.983
Just make a new life.

473
00:29:43.867 --> 00:29:44.952
Yeah. you know…

474
00:29:45.035 --> 00:29:46.245
[sighs]

475
00:29:46.328 --> 00:29:48.080
Thanks. man. but LA's home for me.

476
00:29:49.289 --> 00:29:51.667
Don't do that. After everything?
Just to be given this?

477
00:29:53.293 --> 00:29:54.628
Please.

478
00:29:54.711 --> 00:29:56.380
- [sighs]
- Take it and walk.

479
00:29:59.883 --> 00:30:02.135
- Where the hell is Ji?
- I said we're not doing that.

480
00:30:02.219 --> 00:30:04.888
Then I'm gonna go back to County.
I'm gonna open up Danny's cell.

481
00:30:04.972 --> 00:30:06.598
and I'm gonna ring the dinner bell.
How's that?

482
00:30:06.682 --> 00:30:08.851
And I hang on to Ji.
And you take your chances

483
00:30:08.934 --> 00:30:11.270
that his testimony doesn't put you away
for the rest of your life.

484
00:30:12.354 --> 00:30:13.814
There's no sheriff guards in state prison.

485
00:30:13.897 --> 00:30:15.941
You're gonna be real popular
in Pelican Bay.

486
00:30:19.361 --> 00:30:21.071
[sighs]

487
00:30:21.738 --> 00:30:23.031
So. what do we do?

488
00:30:25.868 --> 00:30:26.869
Oh.

489
00:30:27.452 --> 00:30:28.787
Oh. look. there's your friend.

490
00:30:31.373 --> 00:30:32.708
I wonder what she wants. huh?

491
00:30:32.791 --> 00:30:33.876
She can wait.

492
00:30:37.129 --> 00:30:38.547
Nah. you know what? [sighs]

493
00:30:38.630 --> 00:30:40.132
Let's put a pin in it for now.

494
00:30:41.175 --> 00:30:43.802
She looks worried.
Maybe you guys should talk. you know?

495
00:30:43.886 --> 00:30:45.179
Ray.

496
00:30:46.138 --> 00:30:48.056
All right. I'll see you around. pal.

497
00:30:52.019 --> 00:30:53.228
Last chance.

498
00:30:53.312 --> 00:30:56.982
You know. you keep saying that.
but I don't think so.

499
00:30:57.065 --> 00:30:59.067
[tense music playing]

500
00:31:16.752 --> 00:31:20.672
[no audible dialogue]

501
00:31:21.256 --> 00:31:23.008
- …video games--
- You were playing video games?

502
00:31:23.091 --> 00:31:25.719
- It was the one thing I asked you to do.
- I know. I'm so sorry.

503
00:31:26.261 --> 00:31:27.930
[stammers] It's all right.
We're gonna have to…

504
00:31:30.057 --> 00:31:32.935
He could be… He could be anywhere.

505
00:31:33.018 --> 00:31:34.853
All right. we're just gonna have to
go back to square one.

506
00:31:34.937 --> 00:31:37.689
We're gonna have to go to
all the places that he… he frequented.

507
00:31:37.773 --> 00:31:40.359
places he scored drugs.
the pool hall. wherever.

508
00:31:42.986 --> 00:31:45.239
[officer] Well. you were right.
They lost him.

509
00:31:46.573 --> 00:31:47.574
Play it again.

510
00:31:48.325 --> 00:31:49.910
- The whole thing?
- Play it again.

511
00:31:53.789 --> 00:31:55.499
- [John] What are you doing?
- [Val] He's gone.

512
00:31:55.582 --> 00:31:57.626
- [John] What do you mean he's gone?
- I mean. he fuckin' left.

513
00:31:57.709 --> 00:31:58.877
He took my car. He's gone.

514
00:31:59.378 --> 00:32:01.338
[John] Val. you were
supposed to watch him.

515
00:32:01.421 --> 00:32:02.422
[Val] I know. I'm so sorry.

516
00:32:02.506 --> 00:32:05.384
[stammering] I was watching him
and then we stayed up really late.

517
00:32:05.467 --> 00:32:07.594
- We were playing video games--
- You were playing video games?

518
00:32:07.678 --> 00:32:10.138
- It was the one thing I asked you to do.
- [Val] I know. I'm so sorry.

519
00:32:10.848 --> 00:32:11.849
- Boss.
- [John] It's all right.

520
00:32:11.932 --> 00:32:13.308
- We gonna have to…
- Phone call.

521
00:32:14.852 --> 00:32:15.853
[John] He could be…

522
00:32:15.936 --> 00:32:17.479
Lieutenant Vega.

523
00:32:17.563 --> 00:32:18.814
[Ji] What's your number?

524
00:32:19.690 --> 00:32:21.149
Who am I speaking with?

525
00:32:21.233 --> 00:32:22.484
You know.

526
00:32:22.568 --> 00:32:24.653
Give me your number.
I'm gonna video call you.

527
00:32:26.738 --> 00:32:29.616
[phone ringing]

528
00:32:29.700 --> 00:32:32.035
Hey. Nice to see you again.

529
00:32:32.119 --> 00:32:33.120
I bet.

530
00:32:34.329 --> 00:32:35.747
Thought you were with Sugar.

531
00:32:36.373 --> 00:32:38.208
- Nope.
- Well. where's he at?

532
00:32:38.292 --> 00:32:40.919
Fuck him. Fuck you. Fuck me.

533
00:32:42.212 --> 00:32:43.463
[Vega] Okay.

534
00:32:44.339 --> 00:32:45.340
[sighs]

535
00:32:45.966 --> 00:32:48.302
I'm so tired of this shit. man.

536
00:32:48.886 --> 00:32:51.388
Being the loser fuckin' fuckup.

537
00:32:53.223 --> 00:32:57.144
One time. one fucking time
I wanna do something right.

538
00:32:57.227 --> 00:32:59.980
That sounds good. What are you…
What are you thinking?

539
00:33:00.063 --> 00:33:01.148
You want a trade?

540
00:33:02.024 --> 00:33:03.317
Let's trade.

541
00:33:03.400 --> 00:33:04.735
Me for my brother.

542
00:33:05.319 --> 00:33:10.157
No tricks. no. like.
fuckin' double crosses.

543
00:33:10.240 --> 00:33:12.743
Just me and you and Danny.

544
00:33:13.952 --> 00:33:15.245
Well. that seems fair.

545
00:33:18.081 --> 00:33:19.416
Where you at. bud?

546
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:22.002
[suspenseful music playing]

547
00:33:45.526 --> 00:33:47.694
Hey. sorry about your brother. It sucks.

548
00:33:52.449 --> 00:33:55.911
To be real though. this is. uh.
sort of him trying to do right by you.

549
00:33:55.994 --> 00:33:57.287
you know. which you gotta respect.

550
00:33:58.956 --> 00:34:01.542
Sort of a dying wish sort of thing.
you know?

551
00:34:04.878 --> 00:34:06.129
[screaming]

552
00:34:06.213 --> 00:34:08.215
- [tires screeching]
- [Vega] Jesus Christ!

553
00:34:13.804 --> 00:34:15.389
- [Vega] What the fuck are you doing?
- [grunts]

554
00:34:15.973 --> 00:34:17.349
You're gonna hurt yourself.

555
00:34:18.225 --> 00:34:20.226
[panting]

556
00:34:37.286 --> 00:34:39.830
[grunting]

557
00:34:42.373 --> 00:34:43.583
How's that? Better?

558
00:35:04.980 --> 00:35:05.981
[Vega sighs]

559
00:35:10.694 --> 00:35:11.945
I'll be right back.

560
00:35:29.213 --> 00:35:30.380
Hey. Ji?

561
00:35:42.643 --> 00:35:45.103
Hey. Your brother's here.

562
00:36:01.578 --> 00:36:02.913
[object clanks]

563
00:36:24.810 --> 00:36:26.812
[objects squeaking]

564
00:36:31.859 --> 00:36:33.735
[squeaking continues]

565
00:36:44.872 --> 00:36:45.873
[door slams]

566
00:36:53.547 --> 00:36:55.048
Fuckin' junkie.

567
00:37:07.269 --> 00:37:08.270
[door closes]

568
00:37:25.329 --> 00:37:27.414
All right. change of plans.

569
00:37:28.790 --> 00:37:30.375
[engine starts]

570
00:37:43.680 --> 00:37:44.765
[Vega] Motherfucker!

571
00:37:44.848 --> 00:37:46.892
[both grunting]

572
00:37:48.101 --> 00:37:49.811
[tires squealing]

573
00:37:55.317 --> 00:37:56.318
[both grunting]

574
00:38:16.171 --> 00:38:18.173
[grunting continues]

575
00:38:35.983 --> 00:38:37.609
[John groans]

576
00:38:42.614 --> 00:38:45.409
[Vega straining. coughing]

577
00:38:53.542 --> 00:38:55.002
[choking. grunting]

578
00:38:55.085 --> 00:38:56.128
[John] I told you.

579
00:38:58.338 --> 00:38:59.965
- [choking]
- I told you.

580
00:39:03.218 --> 00:39:05.137
[panting. choking]

581
00:39:13.520 --> 00:39:15.981
[John panting]

582
00:39:33.874 --> 00:39:36.668
[distorted panting]

583
00:39:49.848 --> 00:39:51.475
[panting]

584
00:40:25.634 --> 00:40:26.718
[Danny] Ji!

585
00:40:28.262 --> 00:40:29.263
[Ji] Danny!

586
00:40:29.346 --> 00:40:31.223
- [Ji. Danny laughing]
- [John panting]

587
00:40:31.306 --> 00:40:33.809
- [hopeful music plays]
- [both clamoring]

588
00:40:36.144 --> 00:40:39.106
[both screaming. laughing]

589
00:40:39.189 --> 00:40:41.900
[Danny] I thought I wasn't gonna
see you again. bro!

590
00:40:42.484 --> 00:40:44.027
- [exclaims]
- [Ji] Hey. what happened?

591
00:40:44.111 --> 00:40:45.988
[Danny] No. I'm okay. I'm okay. I'm okay.

592
00:40:47.322 --> 00:40:49.741
- [Danny cries]
- [Ji] I'm so sorry.

593
00:40:49.825 --> 00:40:51.034
[John breathes heavily]

594
00:41:08.260 --> 00:41:10.262
[chattering on TV]

595
00:41:19.313 --> 00:41:21.940
- [Max Corkle] Okay. Joe. that's enough.
- Come on. Maxie.

596
00:41:22.482 --> 00:41:24.985
Only had five rounds.
Can't I have a couple more?

597
00:41:25.777 --> 00:41:27.321
You heard me. I said that's enough now.

598
00:41:28.447 --> 00:41:31.116
[Tom] Remember.
that's Sheriff's territory.

599
00:41:31.200 --> 00:41:32.201
They'll be listening.

600
00:41:32.284 --> 00:41:33.785
Yeah. Eyes and ears.

601
00:41:33.869 --> 00:41:35.579
[Joe Pendleton]
Cremated. that's what I said.

602
00:41:35.662 --> 00:41:37.289
While you guys kept me up here gabbing.

603
00:41:37.372 --> 00:41:39.541
that Corkle gets my body out of
the plane and has me cremated.

604
00:41:44.004 --> 00:41:46.215
- [John] What do you mean he's gone?
- I mean. he's gone.

605
00:41:46.298 --> 00:41:48.759
- He stole my fuckin' car and he left.
- Val. you were supposed to watch him.

606
00:41:48.842 --> 00:41:51.178
[Val] I know. but fuck. we stayed up
really late playing video games.

607
00:41:51.261 --> 00:41:53.805
- [Mr. Jordan] I'm taking you back.
- Yeah. but you can't.

608
00:41:53.889 --> 00:41:55.682
Didn't we just tell you?
I haven't got a body anymore.

609
00:41:55.766 --> 00:41:57.434
What of it? I'll get you another body.

610
00:41:58.143 --> 00:41:59.686
- You'll do what?
- Another body?

611
00:41:59.770 --> 00:42:01.355
Well. that's what I said.
Come along. Joseph.

612
00:42:01.438 --> 00:42:03.690
No. wait a minute. wait a minute.
What kind of a deal is this?

613
00:42:05.734 --> 00:42:07.236
[messenger 7013]
Couldn't we have him reborn?

614
00:42:09.905 --> 00:42:11.865
[Pendleton]
I'm not going to go through that again.

615
00:42:12.449 --> 00:42:15.369
[Ji] No tricks. okay?
No fuckin'. like. double crosses.

616
00:42:15.452 --> 00:42:17.621
Just me and you and Danny.

617
00:42:17.704 --> 00:42:19.039
[Vega] That seems fair.

618
00:42:19.122 --> 00:42:20.207
Where you at. bud?

619
00:42:36.265 --> 00:42:37.975
I want you to get
in the trunk of that car.

620
00:42:38.058 --> 00:42:38.934
Okay.

621
00:42:41.478 --> 00:42:42.479
[panting]

622
00:42:46.650 --> 00:42:49.486
Mr. Jordan. I've never seen anything
as beautiful as that. not even in heaven.

623
00:42:51.864 --> 00:42:53.198
She's in a tough spot.

624
00:42:53.740 --> 00:42:58.078
Got a lot of courage to come all the way
up here alone to fight for her father.

625
00:42:58.161 --> 00:42:59.246
She worships him.

626
00:43:00.205 --> 00:43:01.874
She's no match for those buzzards.

627
00:43:02.791 --> 00:43:05.544
She needs help. She's in trouble.
You better go to work.

628
00:43:06.044 --> 00:43:08.088
[Pendleton] Farnsworth is the only one
who can help her. Joe.

629
00:43:08.172 --> 00:43:09.464
And he's dead.

630
00:43:10.048 --> 00:43:11.925
[Mr. Jordan] But you can be Farnsworth.

631
00:43:33.071 --> 00:43:34.573
[Peg] You're quiet.

632
00:43:38.577 --> 00:43:40.120
How are you feeling. John?

633
00:43:42.456 --> 00:43:43.540
I'm fine.

634
00:43:45.375 --> 00:43:47.169
You know what this means. right?

635
00:43:50.589 --> 00:43:54.718
I did what I had to do.
[stammers] I had no choice.

636
00:43:57.095 --> 00:44:00.057
[breathes shakily. sighs]

637
00:44:01.099 --> 00:44:02.559
[Charlotte] What'd you say?

638
00:44:03.977 --> 00:44:05.020
Nothing.

639
00:44:07.981 --> 00:44:09.316
Come to bed.

640
00:44:13.362 --> 00:44:15.989
I'm sorry.
I keep on staring at you like this.

641
00:44:16.865 --> 00:44:19.076
That's okay.
I'm doing a little staring myself.

642
00:44:19.576 --> 00:44:20.827
I'm all mixed up.

643
00:44:21.495 --> 00:44:24.248
In fact. I didn't come here
so much to thank you. as to…

644
00:44:25.457 --> 00:44:27.084
Because I had to see you again.

645
00:44:27.960 --> 00:44:29.419
[Pendleton] Well. that's wonderful.

646
00:44:29.920 --> 00:44:31.547
- That's wonderful!
- [Bette Logan] A miracle.

647
00:44:32.297 --> 00:44:33.841
[Pendleton] A miracle? Why?

648
00:44:35.050 --> 00:44:37.719
[Logan] Well. that a man like
Bruce Farnsworth could actually

649
00:44:37.803 --> 00:44:40.389
think the way I was brought up
to think about people.

650
00:44:41.098 --> 00:44:43.600
That he could have a real feeling
for the happiness of others.

651
00:44:44.601 --> 00:44:47.604
[Pendleton] Well. that's as good a way to
go through life as any other. isn't it?

652
00:44:48.146 --> 00:44:49.940
[Logan] Yes. that's all I meant.

653
00:44:51.149 --> 00:44:55.362
Except. when you find that in somebody.
it's a great discovery.

654
00:44:56.029 --> 00:44:58.699
[giggles]
I guess that's why I keep staring.

655
00:44:59.700 --> 00:45:00.784
I can't help it.

656
00:45:01.410 --> 00:45:05.038
I suddenly feel so warm
and alive and happy.

657
00:45:09.084 --> 00:45:13.046
It's something in your eyes
and what's behind them that…

658
00:45:14.131 --> 00:45:16.258
that I keep trying to see.

659
00:45:18.343 --> 00:45:20.345
["666" playing]
